"""Tone-family pulses measured from high speed capable overs, 2026-09-26: real envelopes,
centre tap 1, fitted by alternating least squares with the cells held to plaintext.

`bw500_pulse` serves the narrow-band rows (BW2300 and BW2750 levels 5-6, BW500
level 5). The two here are distinct pulses, not two fits of one: crossed, each
reads the other's rows at -27 dB, which is P8's tail energy.

`P8`, offsets -1024..1024: BW2300's level-8 fit, serving BW2300 and BW2750
levels 7-8 and BW500 level 6 at -54 to -55 dB. 2e-3 of its energy lies beyond
+-512; its true extent past +-1024 is unknown.

`P9`, offsets -1024..1024: BW2300's level-9 fit refitted on BW2750 level 9,
serving levels 9-10 at -73 to -75 dB. Only 7e-5 of its energy lies beyond +-512,
but cutting it there costs a render about 11 dB of residual against the tape.
Whether BW2300's level 9 wants exactly this pulse or a slightly different one is
unknown (the two fits sit -45.7 dB apart).
"""

